# Library words before their value (notes/layers.md, sugar): `reverse xs`, `upper t`, `floor x`, a library word of one
# typed value the program leaves free (lib/prelude.warp, lib/math.warp: `floor(x: number): int from warp`) applies to
# the value after it, as `reverse(xs)` does; a synonym calls its word (`sorted xs`). A word with a default or a rest
# parameter takes no spaced argument. Rust twin: library_words.rs word_call, library_signatures.rs typed_first_arity
rewrite ($f $x) => $f($x) where $f takes one
# before several words it takes the phrase they make: `reverse sort xs` is `reverse(sort xs)`, then `reverse(sort(xs))`
rewrite ($f $x $more...) => $f(($x $more...)) where $f takes one

# Pipes (wiki/pipe.md, decision D6): `x | f` is the call f(x) of a function of the program or a library word of one
# value, `3 | inc | dbl` is dbl(inc(3)); between two functions `|` composes them, `inc | dbl` is `x => x | inc | dbl`,
# and a composition piped on composes, `inc | dbl | square`; between values `|` stays the logical or. Rust twin: pipes.rs
rewrite ($it => $body) | $g => $it => $body | $g where $g is function
rewrite $f | $g => $it => $it | $f | $g where $f is function and $g is function
rewrite $x | $f => $f($x) where $f is function
rewrite $x | $f => $f($x) where $f takes one
